    Present before that slice.
  leaf-covariate-moments-range: standardizationMomentsForColumn takes a
    leaf covariate's sd through plain squares, so a column whose spread
    is above about 1e154 gets sd Inf, the leaf term then reading zero on
    every row, and one whose spread is below about 1e-154, or denormal,
    gets the placeholder 1 as though it held one value. Scaling by a
    power of two, as the rounding test does, fixes both and keeps every
    bit in the normal range. Found 2026-11-07 by the leaf-spread-rounding
    review's probe of the spread test at the ends of the double range.
    Present before that slice.
