  bartcause-thread-default: on bartCause's dbarts-1.0 branch, bcf.R
    computes n.threads from dbarts::guessNumCores() and passes it as
    stated, so where the cores cannot be counted bcf() is refused;
    leave n.threads out of the call to dbarts when the guess is NA.
  bartcause-weighted-draws: bartCause work. A weighted unit's
    counterfactual noise is drawn at sigma / sqrt(w), as its response
    fit has it, and the PATE and SATE noise terms at sigma^2 / sum(w),
    a weight-0 unit drawing NA and counting 0, so an interval no longer
    depends on the weights' scale (dec-B696). About 10 to 20 lines in
    bartCause, tests and NEWS.
  copy-merge-weight-order: after a forced setCutPoints or refresh that
    merges, a copy's merged leaf can differ from its original's by one
    unit in the last place when the leaf's weights do not sum exactly
    (runif weights: 1 run in 10 on arm64, 3 on x86), the merge summing
    weights in each sampler's own row order; exact weights agree.
  refused-update-rounding: after a refused whole-matrix setPredictor
    the next draws differ from an untouched twin's by about 1.8e-15,
    where the help says the fits are as they were.
  precision-floor-edge-values: the floor that refuses scales and
    Polya-Gamma variates that are not positive and finite passes a
    value at the edge of what a double holds: a variate of 1e-320 in a
    logistic or negative-binomial block installs and the next sweep
    does not return, and the largest finite double as a scale gives
    fits that are not finite. No stored state holds such a value; a
    block edited by hand can, within one family as across two
    (docs/plans/state-family-record-removal.md, landing note).
  single-forest-vars-leftovers: the column restriction on a single declared
    forest left one thing (docs/design/single-forest-vars.md): the model's
    forest.columns attribute moves into the first forest's record when the
    control migration gives every model one.
  weighted-binary: arbitrary real weights on the binary families need
    a real-shape Polya-Gamma sampler; IPW is a pseudo-likelihood trap,
    and the approximate-PG decision is shared with
    negbin-real-dispersion. Integer-weight logistic ships via
    replicated latents, and probit refuses weights outright - no
    tractable weighted latent form. docs/plans/weighted-binary.md.
    Scheduled for 1.0-0 under approximate-distributions (dec-B592, which
    revises the 2026-08-28 schedule).
  hurdle-weight-extensions: door, after hurdle-completion and
    frequency-weights (VD 2026-11-03, dec-B588: 0 and 1 now, "think
    about extensions in the future"). A logistic zero part,
    "hurdle.logistic" (docs/design/hurdle.md, Doors), would take
    whole-number weights as counts on both parts with no engine work
    now that frequency weights are built, logistic's Polya-Gamma shape being the
    count and the gaussian positive part taking frequency weights, and
    non-integer counts once an accept-or-keep Polya-Gamma latent exists
    (dec-B583). Its latent costs about four times probit's per row at
    weight 1 and grows with the count, and it has no rescaling step.
    The probit hurdle gains whole numbers with integer-weight probit
    (weighted-binary). Whether logistic becomes the hurdle's default
    is a separate call; pscl defaults to a logit and offers probit.

absolute residual prior scale (decided, VD 2026-09-14)
  post-release, R only: chisq gains an absolute spelling,
  chisq(df, scale = lambda), which names the prior literally instead of
  through the sigest its quantile calibrates against, and ignores
  sigest as fixed() does. Additive - a new argument beside quant, no
  spelling retired, so no tombstone. The residual prior's one home on
  the family object is the surface it is added to (docs/decisions.md
  dec-B123). scheduled after 1.0-0 (VD 2026-09-14).

front-door rename (decided, VD 2026-09-08; docs/decisions.md dec-B75;
  LANDED 2026-09-09; plan docs/plans/front-door.md)
  bart2's removal in 1.1-0 is gated (VD 2026-09-23): before removing
  it, check every CRAN reverse dependency for a bart2 call, and keep the
  alias one more release if any remains. WeightIt and MatchIt call it
  as of 2.0.0 and 4.8.0 (release block).
  Every other tombstone expires at 1.1-0 too (dec-B76; the registry in
  R/tombstones.R, which inst/tinytest/test-tombstones.R fails once the
  version reaches its expiry): in that release delete the file, the
  stubs, forwards and once-per-session warnings it lists, the
  .onAttach message, and their NAMESPACE entries.
  tree.prior leaves with them (tree-prior-flat, D8): its trailing formal
  on dbarts() and dbartsSpec(), the reading of a cgm()/dart() call or a
  tree prior saved by 0.9-34 as plain arguments, and cgm from
  dbartsPriors. The dbartsCGMPrior and dbartsDartPrior classes stay, as
  the record a model holds.

