variable-selection-permutation (VD 2026-09-27; docs/decisions.md dec-A73)
  post-release, gated: Bleich et al. (2014)'s permutation thresholds for
  variable selection (refit on permuted responses, compare inclusion
  proportions against the null; bartMachine's var_selection_by_permute),
  an R function over bart() and extract(type = "varcount") plus a plot.
  First answer whether it is a good idea and used: its standing against
  the DART prior the package already ships and later selection work,
  and evidence of use (citing applications, bartMachine users). Build
  only if that case holds; VD: "we don't need to cram everyone's idea
  into the package."

hurdle feature completion (VD 2026-09-26: part of feature completion,
  not to be forgotten; docs/decisions.md dec-A15; LANDED 2026-11-05;
  plan docs/plans/hurdle-completion.md)
  a hurdle.lognormal fit takes a formula and a data object, a test set
  (a real test channel read by extract and fitted with sample), subset,
  weights of 0 and 1, and offsets: a plain offset enters the positive
  part, offset = list(zero = , positive = ) gives each part its own, as
  pscl::hurdle's offset argument enters the positive part. predict takes
  offset and weights, and pdbart and pd2bart carry each part's offset.
  Still owed elsewhere: whole-number weights (hurdle-weight-extensions,
  above), and the other families' predicts lack the weights formal that
  dec-B580's door to a 0 row's draw needs (frequency weights).

